{
    author: "SlideDeckML Team"
    title: "Synchronized Fragments Test"
}
===
# Sync with line-by-line (Replace Mode)

::: {display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2em; align-items: start}

```javascript [highlight:line-by-line]
let x = 0;
x = x + 5;
x = x * 2;
console.log(x);
```

:::[sync-fragments]
x = 0
[---]
x = 5
[---]
x = 10
[---]
Output: 10
:::[sync-fragments]

:::

===
# Sync with line-by-line (Keep Mode)

::: {display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2em; align-items: start}

```python [highlight:line-by-line]
count = 0
count += 10
count *= 3
print(count)
```

:::[sync-fragments keep]
count = 0
[---]
count = 10
[---]
count = 30
[---]
Output: 30
:::[sync-fragments]

:::

===
# Sync with block highlighting

::: {display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2em; align-items: start}

```java [highlight:block]
String name = "Alice";
int age = 25;

String greeting = "Hello " + name;

System.out.println(greeting);
System.out.println("Age: " + age);
```

:::[sync-fragments]
Variables initialized
[---]
Greeting created
[---]
Output printed
:::[sync-fragments]

:::

===
# Sync with function highlighting

::: {display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2em; align-items: start}

```typescript [highlight:function]
function add(a: number, b: number): number {
    return a + b;
}

function multiply(a: number, b: number): number {
    return a * b;
}
```

:::[sync-fragments keep]
Addition function defined
[---]
Multiplication function defined
:::[sync-fragments]

:::

===
# Sync with class highlighting

::: {display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2em; align-items: start}

```python [highlight:class]
class Animal:
    def __init__(self, name):
        self.name = name
    
    def speak(self):
        pass

class Dog(Animal):
    def speak(self):
        return "Woof!"
```

:::[sync-fragments]
Base class Animal
[---]
Derived class Dog
:::[sync-fragments]

:::

